ced"}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":"16px","color":"#737373","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"May 13, 2026"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"AI in China"}]]}]]}],["$","img",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504639725590-34d0984388bd?w=1200&h=600&fit=crop","alt":"The Invisible Empire: How China's AI Consumer Apps Quietly Conquered 2.5 Billion Users — And Why the World Barely Noticed","style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto","borderRadius":"12px","marginBottom":"48px"}}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511707171634-5f897ff02aa9?w=1200\""}]]}],["$","p","7",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"While Silicon Valley obsessed over GPT-5's next token and Anthropic's march toward a trillion-dollar valuation, something extraordinary was happening on the other side of the Pacific. China's AI consumer apps — the ones Western tech media rarely covers — were quietly assembling an empire of users that rivals the population of India and China combined."}]]}],["$","p","9",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Doubao, ByteDance's AI assistant, crossed 100 million daily active users in February 2026, becoming the first AI-native app in China to reach that milestone. MiniMax, the Shanghai-based startup behind the global hit Talkie, accumulated 2.36 billion total users across more than 200 countries and territories. The entire Chinese AI chatbot ecosystem now serves over 700 million monthly active users. And the engines powering all of this consume 140 trillion tokens every single day — a 1,000-fold increase in just two years."}]]}],["$","p","11",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"This isn't a funding story. This isn't a model benchmark story. This is a story about what happens when AI stops being a research demo and becomes infrastructure for everyday life — and how China, with its unique combination of massive domestic market, mobile-first culture, and aggressive product iteration, built a consumer AI empire that the rest of the world barely noticed."}]]}],["$","hr","13",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","p","15",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Before diving into individual companies and trends, let's establish the magnitude of what we're looking at. China's AI consumer market has reached a scale that demands recalibration of how the global industry measures success."}]]}],["$","div","27",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Metric"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Figure"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Context"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span